  - type: prose
    paragraphs:
      - "Zytro is a 3D visualization company for architecture and real estate, blending architecture, design, and technology to create immersive visuals and digital experiences."
      - "This project was a website relaunch."
      - "The goal was to make the brand feel as contemporary and distinctive as the work itself."
      - "The previous site did not fully communicate the studio’s range, visual ambition, or premium positioning."
      - "The relaunch needed to do that from the first scroll."

  - type: media
    src: "[hero video here]"
    alt: Zytro website hero section
    caption: "Opening section of the relaunch."
    variant: bare
    aspect: "auto"

  - type: heading
    text: The goal

  - type: prose
    paragraphs:
      - "This was not a minimal corporate refresh."
      - "The site had to feel creative, technical, and current."
      - "It needed to elevate brand perception, present services more clearly, and turn the website into a stronger expression of the studio’s identity."
      - "Beauty was part of the strategy."
      - "For a company selling high-end visual work, a generic interface would have weakened the message."
      - "The website itself needed to feel designed."

  - type: heading
    text: Creative direction

  - type: prose
    paragraphs:
      - "The direction was bold and cinematic."
      - "I used a dark interface as the base. Then I introduced soft gradients, glowing details, large-scale type, thin graphic lines, and a more deconstructed layout language."
      - "The result felt digital, architectural, and slightly experimental."
      - "Not chaotic. Controlled."
      - "This gave the relaunch a stronger sense of authorship."

  - type: media
    src: "[creative direction image here]"
    alt: Zytro creative direction
    caption: "The visual direction behind the relaunch."
    variant: bare
    aspect: "auto"

  - type: heading
    text: Section by section

  - type: subheading
    text: Hero

  - type: prose
    paragraphs:
      - "The hero was designed to establish tone immediately."
      - "Large typography, floating devices, graphic symbols, and layered depth helped frame the site as both creative and technical."
      - "It introduced the visual system before the user even started reading."

  - type: media
    src: "[hero section video here]"
    alt: Hero section of Zytro website
    caption: "Hero section."
    variant: bare
    aspect: "auto"

  - type: subheading
    text: Overview

  - type: prose
    paragraphs:
      - "This section balanced atmosphere with clarity."
      - "After the expressive opening, the layout slowed down and explained what Zytro does, why the relaunch mattered, and what kind of experience the visitor could expect."
      - "It was a transition from impression to understanding."

  - type: media
    src: "[overview section video here]"
    alt: Overview section of Zytro website
    caption: "Overview section."
    variant: bare
    aspect: "auto"

  - type: subheading
    text: Work and services

  - type: prose
    paragraphs:
      - "This part focused on showing range without flattening everything into a standard grid."
      - "Cards, tabs, and bento-style compositions helped break the portfolio into more dynamic visual units."
      - "That made the content feel lighter, more engaging, and easier to explore."

  - type: media
    src: "[work section video here]"
    alt: Work and services section of Zytro website
    caption: "Work and services."
    variant: bare
    aspect: "auto"

  - type: subheading
    text: Parallax and motion

  - type: prose
    paragraphs:
      - "Motion was not added as decoration."
      - "Parallax helped control pacing, create contrast between sections, and keep the long-scroll experience visually alive."
      - "It gave the site more rhythm and helped differentiate it from more static agency websites."

  - type: media
    src: "[parallax section video here]"
    alt: Parallax section of Zytro website
    caption: "Parallax and motion."
    variant: bare
    aspect: "auto"

  - type: subheading
    text: Social proof and team

  - type: prose
    paragraphs:
      - "Trust needed to feel integrated into the experience, not pasted onto it."
      - "Client and team sections were designed to support credibility while still matching the site’s visual language."
      - "That mattered because the website needed to feel premium from end to end, even in its quieter sections."

  - type: media
    src: "[clients or team section video here]"
    alt: Social proof or team section of Zytro website
    caption: "Social proof and team."
    variant: bare
    aspect: "auto"

  - type: subheading
    text: CTA and closing

  - type: prose
    paragraphs:
      - "The final sections carried the same visual confidence as the opening."
      - "Calls to action were treated as part of the composition, not as isolated buttons dropped at the end."
      - "That helped the site finish with the same level of intention it started with."

  - type: media
    src: "[cta or footer video here]"
    alt: CTA and closing section of Zytro website
    caption: "Closing section."
    variant: bare
    aspect: "auto"

  - type: heading
    text: Visual system

  - type: prose
    paragraphs:
      - "The visual language relied on contrast."
      - "Dark backgrounds created depth."
      - "Green and violet accents added distinctiveness."
      - "Large type created presence."
      - "Thin graphic lines and subtle glows added rhythm without overwhelming the layout."
      - "The system was expressive, but still structured."

